{
  "summary": "This experiment tested replacing the ResNet50 image encoder with ViT-L in a multiprofile multimodal setup, maintaining PCA RNA encoding, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion. Validation accuracy improved to 0.6287 (vs 0.6186 in config_004), suggesting the image encoder choice may contribute to performance gains. However, the slightly lower F1 score (0.5993 vs 0.6103) introduces uncertainty about the trade-offs between accuracy and other metrics, and whether this improvement is consistent across different configurations."
}

